  "body": "Shows now uses tracked Vite live reload and a warm four-job Rust cache so edits can be tried before release packaging. The idle stream deadline and missing home signing from my previous remote implementation are corrected; new agent code can be tested locally through the tracked SSH preview bridge, and the final main build is signed before one-command publication and interactive PC updates.\n\nThe development-lifecycle, desktop-distribution, remote-control and round-and-advance contracts preserve NAS authority, immutable verified bundles and normal playback/resume semantics. Verified 0.11-second live source updates, seconds-long changed Rust builds, native preview restart/stop, real cross-PC play/pause, sustained idle status, 114 Rust tests, frontend tests/build, Clippy, publication retry and all three Authenticode signatures.\n\n[SHOWS-3](https://openproject.romaine.life/wp/SHOWS-3)",
